{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Call him, that he may eat bread.</b> Perhaps it means he would marry one of you — in the manner of (Genesis 39): ״כי אם הלחם אשר הוא אוכל״ (for the bread that he eats)." "<b>And by way of the Midrash.</b> In the merit that Jethro said, ״Call him, that he may eat bread,״ he deserved that his sons would sit in the Chamber of Hewn Stone. This is what Solomon, peace be upon him, said (Ecclesiastes 11): ״שלח לחמך על פני המים כי ברוב הימים תמצאנו״ — (another interpretation:) ״Send your bread״ — this is Jethro, who said, ״Call him, that he may eat bread״; ״upon the face of the waters״ — this is Moses, of whom it is said (Exodus 2): ״כי מן המים משיתיהו״; ״for in many days you will find it״ — this is what is written (Exodus 18): ״ויבא אהרן וכל זקני ישראל לאכל לחם״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:21.151848259Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}